      "text": "But first of all, let's talk about the essential years, birth to five years and five to eight years and then into the teenage years because science tells us that during birth to five years of age the neurons are really being laid down then for building a solid architecture for lifelong learning and the stats are magical. A three year old child has developed around 1,000 trillion synapses and gradually over the years the brain makes connections and patterns with them. So by adolescence these connections start to shape the brain and of course there's 500 trillion synapses, trillion normally. So it's a big job to build all of that and certainly what we need to do before children go to school is to build wonderful vocabulary for them.",
