      "start": 164.02,
      "end": 229.95,
      "duration": 65.93,
      "text": "As we do life together we can be building children's vital neurological and language assets for literacy and for speaking and listening. So it's communities who upskill children in basic speech therapy, it's communities who do this and the Australian model shows as a reference how we can work together to do that. It starts with really little ones as you can see and then we build and build and build as a year gets to go on. There is a low or no access to speech and language pathology or speech therapy services around the world and for many reasons children increasingly are needing more and more speech pathology services. So in order to do think that through we need to think through how communities can actually take on that role and provide the basics to fill in and it won't take over from you know the professional speech therapy services.",
